1) Concurrency of sibling tool calls in one assistant message
CONCURRENT by default. `.../pi-agent-core/dist/agent-loop.js:286-291`:
```js
const hasSequentialToolCall = toolCalls.some((tc) => currentContext.tools?.find((t) => t.name === tc.name)?.executionMode === "sequential");
if (config.toolExecution === "sequential" || hasSequentialToolCall) {
    return executeToolCallsSequential(...);
}
return executeToolCallsParallel(...);
```
The parallel executor runs all prepared calls together — `agent-loop.js:372`:
```js
const orderedFinalizedCalls = await Promise.all(finalizedCalls.map((entry) => (typeof entry === "function" ? entry() : Promise.resolve(entry))));
```
The sequential executor awaits each call in order — `agent-loop.js:296,313`:
```js
for (const toolCall of toolCalls) {
...
const executed = await executePreparedToolCall(preparation, signal, emit);
```
